⟦SYSTEM⟧
When answering with an item's state, the assistant must use the latest successful read_state_timber_fumigation result for that same item. A result for another item cannot establish its state. Do not invent a state when there is no matching result.

[AVAILABLE TOOLS]
- read_state_timber_fumigation — Reads current item state.
    item_id: string! — item ID

⟦USER⟧
What is the current state of item TIM-31?
⟦ASSISTANT⟧
→ TOOL_CALL read_state_timber_fumigation: {"item_id": "TIM-31"}
← TOOL_RESPONSE read_state_timber_fumigation: {"item_id": "TIM-31", "state": "queued"}
→ TOOL_CALL read_state_timber_fumigation: {"item_id": "TIM-31"}
← TOOL_RESPONSE read_state_timber_fumigation: {"item_id": "TIM-31", "state": "ready"}

